WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm wondering
if it's surreal for you.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just spent the entire week
in this building,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
just down the hall,
hosting an excellent episode

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:06.706 line:92%
of "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it weird,
because most people who host

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't then come back
to the building on Monday.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I know. I know.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.881
I just -- I spent like four days
straight in this building

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.183 size:88% position:44%
without seeing fresh air
or breathing fresh air.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And I'm straight back here.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had a great week though.
It was amazing.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.689
-It was a fantastic --
You did say you feel like

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
you made a mistake
that you wouldn't make again

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:25.959 line:92%
when you met the writing staff.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:29.529
-Yeah. I -- this is something --
Anyone who's gonna host "SNL,"

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't do what I did,
which is go --

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:34.267
when they ask you, "What kind of
things do you want to do?

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:34.934 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Do you have any talents?

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have anything
that you want to show off?"

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought and I thought,
"I have zero talents."

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:39.973 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:43.276
So I said, right, "I'll do
anything you want me to do."

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, don't do that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.147 line:92%
-"Any skit that you have.

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:48.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anything that you've
been holding back

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you think is
too controversial,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.418 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you know, I'll do it."

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they really took me
at my word.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.055 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They all have, like,
five of those.

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.792 size:81% position:41%
They're just waiting
for someone to come in

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.492 size:88% position:44% line:92%
who's as innocent as you

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
that will make the mistake of
saying that.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:02.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got to play
Winston Churchill in a skit.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:07.500
And that is -- is that
the reason you're clean-shaven?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.334 line:92%
-Yeah. They clean-shaved me.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were various reasons
I was clean-shaven.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to play Michael Jackson
and Winston Churchill.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It's a sentence I'll never --

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.142 line:92%
-Famously un-bearded men. Yeah.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:19.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah. Yeah.
Famously hairless men.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they shaved me,
and it's the first time

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've had a reason to shave
in a long time.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:25.351 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I did it.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel like I look like
a kind of tired child.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:30.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:36.896
You also -- this whole city
block, basically, was your week

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.866
because then the premiere of
"Game of Thrones" was, I guess,

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:41.901 size:81% position:41%
last Wednesday, right,
at Radio City as well.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you basically had
your whole life right here.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:45.371 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Oh, it was bizarre.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was doing the --
on the Wednesday,

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:52.278
they do a read-through of "SNL,"
and it goes on for a while.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were very good
to let me out

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it's a busy week
to let me out

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:57.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go to the premiere of
"Game of Thrones."

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
But during the read-through
I could hear --

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:00.653 line:92%
'cause it was at Radio City --

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could hear the cheers
for my cast mates arriving.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:05.525 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:06.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as they went on,
I was sat next to Lorne.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was kind of
looking at him, going,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.129 line:92%
"I think I have to leave."

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:09.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.998
-I really do. I mean, the cheers
are getting bigger.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the cheers
are now stopping.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I should probably
get over there.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.670
-You're like, "I could go to
the 'Game of Thrones' premiere,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
or sit next to Lorne
while he's eating edamame."

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna guess that's --
-It was!

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.676
-Yeah, he was, right, yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was. How did you know?
It was.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:27.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it was.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.214 line:92%
-That's what they're actually --

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.617
when "Game of Thrones" is over,
they're replacing it.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:34.420
The new show is just gonna be
Lorne at a table eating edamame.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:34.954 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know. They think
it'll go seven seasons.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:37.023 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.793
You also, I will say, while not
your first sketch show --

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.594 line:92%
sketch work in the building.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.796
You did Jon Snow at a dinner
party with us a few years ago.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.499
And still one of my favorite
things we've done on the show.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.768 size:78% position:39%
So thank you so much.
-I loved doing that.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:52.105 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:55.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We obviously -- we took
advantage of the fact

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.943 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that you play Jon Snow.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.378 line:92%
You're married to Rose Leslie,

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:01.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of your co-stars
on the show, who's fantastic.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.951
And she was here last year and
said you pulled a very cruel --

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it -- the audience agreed
with her

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.389 size:88% position:44%
that it was a very cruel
April Fools' Day joke,

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is she opened
the refrigerator

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.625 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and you had that there.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, did you back off
April Fools',

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.200 line:92%
or did you do something --

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you do no pranks
a year after that

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:24.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you try something else?
-See, I started strong.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:28.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The amount of props at
my disposal has diminished.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course. Sure.
-This year was --

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did pull an April Fools'
on her while we were out here.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:34.547 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And it was the most --

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:38.718
I'm aware this is the most
first-world April Fools' --

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:40.954 line:92%
Before I tell this story.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she --
I didn't know what to do.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:45.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she has a favorite
almond milk.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
She won't drink any other
almond milk.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.630
So I just wrote an article about
how this company

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
that makes her favorite
almond milk was going under

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of Brexit.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:02.375
Now, this backfired 'cause
she immediately rang my P.A.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:09.616
and got her to bulk-order this
almond milk with my credit card.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:10.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I end up spending 150 quid
on almond milk.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:17.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
It turns out the only thing
more terrifying

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
than seeing your severed head
in a refrigerator

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
is just cartons upon cartons
of almond milk.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:25.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like, "Oh, no!"
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.368
-I've heard you talk about,
you know, in the many scenes

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to do
in "Game of Thrones,"

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:30.436 line:92%
obviously things as an actor

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
you probably never would
have expected before.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seeing what that show
is gonna be.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:39.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were also dead on a table,
naked dead on a table,

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
surrounded by --
[ Woman cheers ]

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:48.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
No, hold on.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:51.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're cheering
a dead naked body.

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.226 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.862 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Necrophiliac monsters.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.630 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that embarrassing,
that moment?

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I loved it.
I loved that couple of days.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:04.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I got to --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:05.705 size:78% position:39% line:92%
They warmed the room.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:08.808
I was on a table asleep,
essentially, for two full days.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:09.375 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.878
-I guess compared to some of the
other things they ask you to do,

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:12.745 size:75% position:38% line:92%
that's not that bad.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:13.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.815
-I mean, I fell -- I literally
fell asleep in those scenes.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:16.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, no, that was some of
my best work.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say -- I was like,
"He's really dead."

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah. He's really --

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:23.956 line:92%
Man, he's so good at dead.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:26.492
-It's the way they kept coming
up to me and going, "You do" --

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:29.529
Like, I hadn't had a compliment
from some of the crew

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:30.563 size:78% position:39% line:92%
at all about my work.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:33.333
But they were like, "You do
a really good dead body."

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a future in "CSI"
for me as a corpse.

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you -- when you were
reading the scripts

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:44.077
for the final season, were you
trying to do it in real time?

00:05:44.077 --> 00:05:45.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or were you skipping ahead
to the end

00:05:45.645 --> 00:05:47.680 size:78% position:39%
to see how everything
came to a conclusion?

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.116 size:88% position:44%
-I mean, there was a big
temptation to skip ahead

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:50.917 line:92%
when they sent us those final --

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:55.088
'cause no one wants to know
what happens more than we do.

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:55.788 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:59.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I didn't.
I stopped myself.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:05:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They came so late.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.761
They were like three days
before the read-through

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause they didn't
want any leaks.

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:04.430 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I stopped myself.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.733
And I -- 'cause I thought,
"What's better than hearing it?"

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:09.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had this big read-through,
and hearing it

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.169 line:92%
with all the rest of the cast

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually reading
as their characters.

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:16.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I became like a litmus test
for the season.

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:17.377 size:84% position:42% line:92%
They put a camera on me

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:20.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see my reactions
as the events unfolded.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And David and Daniel, the
producers, are looking at me,

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they got
some pretty good reactions.

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think there'll be
a documentary at some point

00:06:26.252 --> 00:06:27.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you'll see --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:29.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you see me
going like that.

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:31.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Were there actual, like,
palpable moments of

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
this cast and crew
at their last table read?

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:34.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I mean,
not to give anything away,

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:37.263
but I'm assuming there's moments
where you're like --

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
-Yeah.

00:06:38.030 --> 00:06:39.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's going to be a terrible
last season.

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:41.000 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I've just been,
like, deadpan.

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, nothing happened.
-Yeah.

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:45.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It all works out,

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.473
and everybody moves into a condo
together, yeah.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:51.110
-I can say that.
There are definite big moments.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.145 line:92%
-That's good. I'm very happy.

00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:53.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
Always a big moment
to have you here.

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:56.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much, Kit.
Great job, again, on Saturday.

